    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0432" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20 Mission/7–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-15T17:00:00+03:25">July 15, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—12:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>505. Department’s 407 dated July 4. After consulting with General Ridley who
                    requested that matter be held up one week until his progress report (based on
                    report to Washington dated May 31<anchor n="21" xml:id="d438-f1"/>) had been
                    presented to and read by Iranian Government, I have now handed an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to Prime Minister setting forth War
                    Department’s <pb facs="0433" n="421" xml:id="pg421"/> wishes respecting
                    withdrawal Ridley Mission as of November 1, 1944. Saed promised to take up
                    question with Council of Ministers and let me know immediately his Government’s
                    wishes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
